  "conclusion": "The conjectured n-rate O(1/n) is empirically false: the slope vs log(n) at fixed \u03b2 is far from -1 (typically positive at small \u03b2). The dominant scaling is in \u03b2, not in n. log(mean error) decays approximately linearly in log(\u03b2) at fixed n with decay exponent in [0.4, 0.8] \u2014 i.e. error \u2248 const \u00b7 \u03b2^{-p} with 0.4 \u2264 p \u2264 0.8, consistent with O(\u03b2^{-1/2}) to O(\u03b2^{-1}) Maslov-limit convergence."
